{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>These are the sons of Zilpah… the sons of Rachel, Jacob's wife, etc.</b> The way of Scripture is to enumerate the sons of the handmaids together at the beginning, as it said in the portion of \"And Jacob sent\" (Genesis 35:23–26) and in the portion of \"And these are the names of the children of Israel\" (Exodus 1:2–4), or to enumerate them according to their genealogies — the firstborn according to his birthright and the younger according to his youth — as he did in their blessing in the portion of \"And Jacob lived.\" But here, since it comes to count their number — for with seventy souls they went down to Egypt — he gave precedence to the one most numerous in persons. Therefore he mentioned Rachel in the midst of the handmaids, and it was necessary to mention her with honor, and he said \"Jacob's wife,\" as I mentioned above (Genesis 31:33 [referring to 31:4, 27])."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:45:45.753183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}